From 76c04dd6b7a9937fbaf7eb5a3741aa4e95ad2602 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Markus Volk <f_l_k@t-online.de>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 00:29:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] capture: fall back to KWin's ScreenShot2 D-Bus interface

KWin offers neither wlr-screencopy nor ext-image-copy-capture, so the
screenshot commands fail on KDE sessions. Add a capture backend that asks
org.kde.KWin.ScreenShot2 for the output or area instead and feeds the
raw frame into the existing pipeline. It is only created on KDE and only
used when no screencopy global is present.

KWin authorizes callers by matching their executable against the Exec
line of a desktop entry that lists the interface, so the desktop file
now carries the absolute bindir and X-KDE-DBUS-Restricted-Interfaces.

Signed-off-by: Markus Volk <f_l_k@t-online.de>
